 "note": "Per-(genre, class) verifier agreement on ANLI's verified subset, within R3 only (round held fixed). gold_majority_rate = share of a cell's examples whose writer gold equals the strict verifier majority; gold_support_rate = fraction of that cell's individual verifier votes equalling the writer gold; unanimous_rate = share of lines on which all verifiers agree. P1 (structural, finding either way) bets gold == strict majority on >99% in EVERY cell with >=100 R3 examples. P2 (directional, finding either way) bets that WITHIN R3 neutral is the least decisively verified class (lowest gold_support_rate) in at least 4 of the 6 genres -- testing whether the 'neutral is hardest' class effect of audits 42/44/45 is robust across text domains once the round is fixed. P3 (cross-check) reproduces audits 39/48/49 (gold == strict majority on 29,765 of 29,803 joined lines). Measures AGREEMENT, not correctness."
